3. How AI Assisted Throughout the Implementation
AI was used as a development assistant during the creation of the application. It helped with planning the project structure, understanding React concepts, and improving development efficiency.
AI assistance included:
•	Generating ideas for application features. 
•	Suggesting a component-based React structure. 
•	Explaining React hooks such as useState and useEffect. 
•	Helping create game logic for checking winners and draws. 
•	Identifying coding issues and suggesting fixes. 
•	Providing recommendations for improving UI design and responsiveness. 
•	Reviewing code quality and suggesting refactoring opportunities. 
The generated suggestions were reviewed, tested, and modified before being included in the final application.
________________________________________
4. Manual Improvements, Corrections, and Refactoring
After reviewing AI-generated code, several manual improvements were made:
State Management Improvements
•	Fixed state updates that were being triggered during component rendering. 
•	Moved score updates into a proper React lifecycle using useEffect. 
•	Improved handling of game states such as winner, draw, and active turns. 
Code Refactoring
•	Organized game logic into reusable functions. 
•	Improved variable and function names for better readability. 
•	Reduced repeated code by creating reusable components. 
•	Separated UI components from game logic. 
UI Improvements
•	Customized the design with a unique color theme. 
•	Added responsive sizing for different screen sizes. 
•	Added hover effects and winning-square highlights. 
•	Improved button styling and user feedback messages. 
Bug Fixes
•	Corrected CSS formatting issues. 
•	Improved draw detection handling. 
•	Ensured scores update correctly after each round. 
•	Prevented players from selecting already filled squares. 
________________________________________
Conclusion:
AI was used as a support tool throughout the development process, helping with planning, debugging, and improving the application. The final application was reviewed, modified, and enhanced manually to ensure better functionality, code quality, and user experience.

